        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best protein chip is the one that delivers the most complete protein per calorie without piling on sodium, and on the label that is Quest's tortilla-style range: about 19 g of milk and whey isolate protein for 140 calories, with the lowest sodium per gram of protein here. It was also the cheapest per gram on Amazon when we checked. Twin Peaks is the leanest choice, Legendary packs the most protein into one bag, Pure Protein is the plant-based crisp and Wilde is the dairy-free option.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep protein chips in their lane. They are an excellent replacement for a bag of ordinary chips and a poor replacement for a cheap scoop of powder. Read the sodium line before the protein line, compare protein per 100 calories, buy multipacks sold by Amazon or the brand, and if the crunch is what you are after rather than the flavor, try dry-roasted edamame for a fraction of the price.
          </p>
